<After_two_idle_years_in_Linz,_in_October_1907_Hitler_left_his_mother_(who_was_incurably_ill_with_cancer)_and_moved_to_Vienna,_where_he_remained_until_1913_leading_a_bohemian_existence,_making_a_precarious_living_selling_paintings_and_drawings_of_Vienna_and_producing_posters_and_advertisements_for_small_traders.> <base.kwebbase.kwsentence.next_sentence> "During this Vienna period (1907-13), Hitler read a great deal and absorbed many of the anti-Semitic, anti-liberal and anti-democratic ideas then common in Austria,  spread by, amongst others, the defrocked monk, Lanz von Liebenfels (whose theory of \'Theozoology\' divided humanity into two groups - Aryan supermen and animal subhumans), and the Austrian Pan-German leader, Georg von Schoenerer." .
