<From_these_and_other_sources,_the_young_Hitler_began_to_construct_a_vision_of_the_world_in_which_Jews_(by_race,_rather_than_by_religion)_became_the_symbol_and_cause_of_all_chaos,_corruption,_and_destruction_in_culture,_politics_and_the_economy,_and_that_the_press,_prostitution,_syphilis,_capitalism,_Marxism,_democracy_and_pacificism_were_all_means_exploited_by_'the_Jew'_in_his_conspiracy_to_undermine_the_German_nation_and_the_purity_of_the_creative_Aryan_race.> <base.kwebbase.kwsentence.previous_sentence> "During this Vienna period (1907-13), Hitler read a great deal and absorbed many of the anti-Semitic, anti-liberal and anti-democratic ideas then common in Austria,  spread by, amongst others, the defrocked monk, Lanz von Liebenfels (whose theory of \'Theozoology\' divided humanity into two groups - Aryan supermen and animal subhumans), and the Austrian Pan-German leader, Georg von Schoenerer." .
